{"id": "EUVD-2026-108714", "enisaUuid": "ff35a634-2dec-3a72-8bcc-7ec47d308fd9", "description": "Aider through 0.86.2 contains a command execution vulnerability that allows attackers to run shell commands by committing a malicious .aider.conf.yml that is auto-loaded without a trust prompt. Attackers can set notifications-command or editor values that are executed via subprocess with shell=True after model replies or /editor use, running commands with the victim's privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:36:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:36:49", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/issues/5885", "https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/blob/v0.86.2/aider/io.py#L1088-L1094", "https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/blob/v0.86.2/aider/editor.py#L89-L134", "https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/blob/v0.86.2/aider/main.py#L464-L479", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/aider-through-0.86.2-command-execution-via-repository-aider-conf-yml-settings"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115726"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6ad5a68c-1fd6-3232-8224-3214eeabab64", "product": {"name": "Aider", "vendor": {"name": "Aider-AI"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.86.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "37ae16f3-2fe8-3070-85c3-aa3e4c0c3f55", "vendor": {"name": "Aider-AI"}}], "isExploited": false}